17	PO5	Excel in both individual and team roles within diverse and multidisciplinary settings, while communicating complex computer science concepts clearly through effective reports, presentations, and interactions.	2
18	PO6	Apply engineering and management principles to lead and manage projects effectively in computer science contexts.	2
19	PO7	Embrace and actively pursue continuous learning to stay current with technological advancements and evolving practices in computer science.	2
20	PO1	Demonstrate a solid foundation in computer application principles, critical problem analysis, and solution design, with the ability to conduct thorough investigations and address complex technical challenges.	4
21	PO2	Create, select, and apply advanced techniques, resources, and IT tools for complex computer application tasks, with an understanding of their limitations and applications.	4
22	PO3	Evaluate and address societal, health, safety, legal, and cultural issues related to computing, considering the environmental impact of solutions and advocating for sustainable practices.	4
23	PO4	Apply ethical principles and adhere to professional ethics and norms in the practice of computer applications.	4
24	PO5	Excel in both individual and team roles in diverse and multidisciplinary environments, effectively communicating complex computer application concepts through reports, presentations, and interactions.	4
25	PO6	Utilize management principles to lead and manage projects effectively within computer applications contexts.	4
26	PO7	Engage in continuous learning to stay updated with technological advancements and evolving practices in computer applications.	4
1	PO1	Engineering Knowledge: Apply knowledge of mathematics, science and engineering fundamentals	1
2	PO2	Problem Analysis: Identify, formulate and analyse complex engineering problems	1
3	PO3	Design/Development: Design solutions for complex engineering problems	1
4	PO4	Conduct Investigations: Use research-based knowledge to investigate complex problems	1
5	PO5	Modern Tool Usage: Apply appropriate techniques and modern engineering tools	1
6	PO6	The Engineer and Society: Apply contextual knowledge to assess societal issues	1
7	PO7	Environment and Sustainability: Understand the impact of professional engineering solutions	1
8	PO8	Ethics: Apply ethical principles and commit to professional ethics	1
9	PO9	Individual and Team Work: Function effectively as an individual and in teams	1
10	PO10	Communication: Communicate effectively on complex engineering activities	1
11	PO11	Project Management: Demonstrate knowledge and understanding of management principles	1
12	PO12	Life-long Learning: Recognize the need for self-directed lifelong learning	1
13	PO1	Graduates will possess a strong foundation in computer science principles, critical problem analysis, and solution design, equipped with skills for conducting thorough investigations to solve complex challenges.	2
14	PO2	Create, select, and apply appropriate techniques, resources, and modern IT tools including prediction and modeling to complex computer science activities with an understanding of the limitations.	2
15	PO3	Apply contextual knowledge to evaluate societal, health, safety, legal, and cultural issues, while under- standing the impact of engineering solutions on the environment and advocating for sustainable development.	2
16	PO4	Apply ethical principles and commit to professional ethics and responsibilities and norms of the computer science practice.	2
